#Salvrest
#gets ready for resting

module Salvrest

#keep those spells going!
# Spell[401].timeleft is Lich's own internally-tracked duration -- it only gets
# updated by a background sync thread matching the game's live Active Spells
# feed back to Lich's spell list by name, and that sync can silently never
# populate a given spell (no error, just stays at its class default of 0,
# which is always < 30). Confirmed live: fired right after a Dreavening should
# have put Elemental Defense I (401) at ~4:10 remaining. Effects::Spells.time_left
# reads straight from the game's live Active Spells dialog feed instead, same
# pattern eloot.lic/ewaggle.lic/BlackArts.lic/bigshot.lic already use for this.
multifput "stow all", "get bottle", "turn bottle", "eat pill", "stow bottle" if Effects::Spells.time_left("Elemental Defense I") < 30

end #End of module
